# Drafted by Gemini (R14 clues), edited.

~ altar
if flag.altar_open
Narrator: The heavy altar stone stands slid forward on iron rollers, exposing a dark shaft that breathes a cold, coppery draft up through the scent of crushed roses.
else
Narrator: Red candles weep tallow over heaps of fresh-cut crimson roses, their thorns glistening in the dim red light that falls through the high cathedral glass.
endif
* [if flag.chalice_found and not flag.altar_open] Use the chalice. -> chalice
* [if not flag.chalice_found] [Perception DC 17] Search the altar. -> found | miss
* [if flag.way_down_known and not flag.chalice_found] Use what we were told. -> found
* [if not flag.chalice_found] Wait for the Evening bell and watch an acolyte tend it. -> found
* Leave. -> END

~ miss
Narrator: Your fingers find only damp velvet, bruised petals, and warm wax; if the stone hides a latch, it keeps its counsel beneath the thorns.
-> altar

~ found
Narrator: Tucked into a niche behind the velvet dossal sits a heavy silver chalice, its bowl ringed with a dry rust that does not smell of wine.
set chalice_found
quest crimson_monastery the_way_down
-> chalice

~ chalice
Narrator: The chalice rests upon a sunken brass plate behind the stone; the counterweight requires a full pint's weight of warm blood to trip the catch.
* Fill it with a hero's own blood. -> own_blood
* Ask a willing faithful for a pint. -> faithful_blood
* Leave. -> END

~ own_blood
Narrator: A blade parts skin, and dark blood patters against the silver bowl until the cold metal drinks its fill.
damage 2d6 necrotic
-> open_altar

~ faithful_blood
faithful_novice [smile]: For the Crimson Rose, and for her altar? Take what she asks of me, friend, and let my vein be blessed.
Narrator: The novice rolls back a sleeve with trembling pride and watches the silver brim without a single flinch.
set crimson_devotions += 1
-> open_altar

~ open_altar
Narrator: The brimming cup sinks into the brass cradle with a greased click, and deep within the stone a hidden chain begins to groan.
set altar_open
quest crimson_monastery holy_vein
cutscene mon_way_down
cutscene mon_way_down_2
-> END

~ pulpit
Narrator: The stone pulpit is carved in the likeness of climbing briars, its lectern worn smooth by gloved hands and dusted with dried petals.
-> END

~ bell_gate
Narrator: A heavy iron grille bars the stair to the bell tower, its lock oiled and stout; from high above comes the leathery rustle of roosting wings.
* [if item:skeleton_key] Use a skeleton key. -> gate_open
* [Sleight of Hand DC 15] Pick it. -> gate_open | gate_miss
* [Athletics DC 17] Force it. -> gate_force | gate_miss
* [if flag.cathedral_audience_done and standing.crimson_faith >= 3] Show the Abbot's invitation. -> gate_open
* Leave. -> END

~ gate_miss
Narrator: Iron grates against stone, stubborn and loud in the stairwell, and the bolt refuses to yield.
-> bell_gate

~ gate_force
Narrator: With a sharp wrench of iron against stone, the lock gives way with a ring that echoes up the tower steps.
set crimson_infractions += 1
standing crimson_faith -1
-> gate_open

~ gate_open
Narrator: The iron grille swings inward, letting down a draft of mountain wind and the sour smell of the belfry.
set bell_gate_open
-> END

~ workbook
Narrator: A grease-stained ledger lies open on the butcher's block, smelling of old tallow and iron. Inside are recipes for binding bat hounds, tempering blades in blood, drawing life from one soul into another, and a note that the Abbot descends alone at the Witching Hour.
give jaegers_workbook
set src_workbook
-> END

~ scriptorium
Narrator: Rows of high oak lecterns stand under red-leaded glass, each holding a volume chained by the spine. The parchment smells of gall ink and dry rose petals.
* [Investigation DC 13] Search the shelves. -> scrip_ok | scrip_miss
* Read slowly through a long watch. -> scrip_ok
* Take the books. -> scrip_take
* Leave. -> END

~ scrip_ok
Narrator: Behind the common hymnals sits a treatise penned in a finer hand. It names a chamber beneath the sanctuary altar called the Bloody Sanctum, reached Only when the Holy Vein is opened.
set src_scriptorium
set way_down_known
quest crimson_monastery the_way_down
-> scriptorium

~ scrip_miss
Narrator: You turn page after stiff page of liturgical chants and lists of tithed silver, finding nothing more than tired eyes.
-> scriptorium

~ scrip_take
Narrator: You slip the finest illuminated testament and a box of brass nibs into your pack while the room keeps its silence.
give rosen_testament
give calligraphers_set
-> scriptorium

~ missal
Narrator: Friar Olaf's personal missal is bound in red velvet worn bald at the corners. Its margins describe the chalice rite and how the three priors were anointed in the hidden vault directly under the high altar.
give olafs_missal
set src_missal
set way_down_known
quest crimson_monastery the_way_down
-> END

~ trophy_chest
Narrator: An iron-banded chest sits at the foot of Cromwell's bed, fastened with a heavy warded padlock.
* [if item:skeleton_key] Use a skeleton key. -> chest_open
* [Sleight of Hand DC 15] Pick it. -> chest_open | chest_miss
* [Athletics DC 17] Break it open. -> chest_open | chest_miss
* Leave. -> END

~ chest_miss
Narrator: The iron hasp groans slightly under {name}'s touch, but the tumblers refuse to yield.
-> trophy_chest

~ chest_open
Narrator: The lock snaps back, revealing a cedar jewel box heaped with loose rubies, cut diamonds, and heavy silver coin taken from the condemned.
give jewel_box_cromwell
gold +500
set crimson_infractions += 1
standing crimson_faith -1
-> END

~ sanctum_door
Narrator: The heavy stone slab hums against your knuckles, sealed tight by a spell that tastes of cold iron.
* [Athletics DC 13] Push it. -> door_open | door_miss
* Shove it together for ten minutes. -> door_open
* Leave. -> END

~ door_miss
Narrator: Your boots scrape on the flagstones, and the warded stone does not budge a hair.
-> sanctum_door

~ door_open
Narrator: With a low groan of grinding rock, the seal snaps and the slab scrapes open into the dark.
set sanctum_door_open
quest crimson_monastery holy_vein
-> END

~ vein_warning
Narrator: Three feet of warm, thick blood sloshes below, rising with a sweet copper stench that turns a living stomach.
* [Religion DC 13] Recall the old rites for a blood-thing. -> vein_holy | vein_none
* Leave. -> END

~ vein_holy
Narrator: An old rubric comes back to you: a single vial of blessed water will curdle a living blood-well to ash.
set vein_warned
-> END

~ vein_none
Narrator: No prayer or page comes to mind, though Axel Farley and his people down here might know the trick of it.
set vein_warned
-> END

~ journal
Narrator: A leather-bound journal rests upon the cold stone of the altar, its pages warped by damp and candle tallow.
* Take it and read it through. -> journal_read
* Take it. -> journal_take

~ journal_read
Narrator: You turn the stiff pages, and the abbot's old hand speaks out of a gentler time.
cutscene mon_knights_tale
cutscene mon_knights_tale_2
cutscene mon_knights_tale_3
-> journal_take

~ journal_take
Narrator: You tuck the heavy book away before the chill can have it back.
give renathyr_journal
set renathyr_journal
-> END

~ painting
Narrator: From a tarnished frame looks an elven woman of quiet grace, her name, Lethica Nightborne, lettered in faded gilt below.
give lethica_painting
set lethica_painting
-> END

~ roses
Narrator: A bundle of black, dried roses lies here, so brittle that the petals crumble to dry dust against your thumb.
give dried_roses
set dried_roses
-> END
